---
import Layout from '../layouts/Layout.astro';
import Career from '../components/Career.astro';
import { caseStudies } from '../data/profile';
import './_root.css';
---

<Layout title="Nicholas Fitton | Full-stack engineer & engineering lead candidate">
  <a class="skip-link" href="#main">
    Skip to content
  </a>
  <div class="profile">
    <nav class="navigation" aria-label="Main navigation">
      <a class="wordmark" href="/" aria-label="Nicholas Fitton home">
        nf<span>.</span>
      </a>
      <div>
        <a href="#work">Selected work</a>
        <a href="#experience">Experience</a>
        <a href="#contact">Contact ↗</a>
      </div>
    </nav>
    <main id="main">
      <header class="hero">
        <p class="eyebrow">
          <span class="status-dot" aria-hidden="true"></span> Open to
          engineering lead roles
        </p>
        <h1>
          Nicholas Fitton<span class="accent">.</span>
        </h1>
        <p class="hero-title">Senior full-stack engineer</p>
        <div class="hero-bottom">
          <div class="intro">
            <p>
              I’m a senior full-stack engineer with experience leading projects
              and managing a small engineering team. I turn broad product
              problems into practical plans, work with stakeholders to shape
              solutions, and deliver alongside the team.
            </p>
            <p>
              I’m looking for an engineering lead role, particularly with a
              company improving people’s working lives or advancing a positive
              environmental mission.
            </p>
          </div>
          <div class="hero-actions">
            <a class="button" href="mailto:resume@nfitton.com">
              Let’s talk <span aria-hidden="true">↗</span>
            </a>
            <a class="text-link" href="/nicholas-fitton-cv.pdf" download>
              Download CV <span class="file-label">PDF · 2 pages</span>
              <span aria-hidden="true">↓</span>
            </a>
            <p class="location">
              Chepstow, South Wales
              <br />
              Remote · Bristol · Cardiff
            </p>
          </div>
        </div>
      </header>
      <section id="work" class="section">
        <div class="section-heading">
          <h2>Selected work</h2>
        </div>
        <div class="case-list">
          {caseStudies.map((study, index) => (
            <article class="case-card">
              <div class="case-meta">
                <span class="case-number">0{index + 1}</span>
                <p class="eyebrow">{study.company}</p>
              </div>
              <div>
                <h3>{study.title}</h3>
                <p>{study.summary}</p>
                <p class="outcome">
                  <span>Outcome</span>
                  {study.outcome}
                </p>
                <a class="text-link" href={`/work/${study.slug}/`}>
                  Read case study <span aria-hidden="true">→</span>
                </a>
              </div>
            </article>
          ))}
        </div>
      </section>
      <section class="section leadership" aria-labelledby="leadership-title">
        <div>
          <h2 id="leadership-title">Management & mentoring</h2>
        </div>
        <div>
          <p>
            As interim engineering manager at OVO, I led a team of four
            including myself while remaining hands-on. In one-to-ones, I
            connected project work with each developer’s interests and career
            goals.
          </p>
          <p>
            With a junior engineer new to React Native, I chose work just beyond
            their current experience. We used whiteboarding to make mathematical
            problems tangible, then paired with them driving the implementation
            and me helping them stay on course.
          </p>
          <p class="outcome">
            <span>Outcome</span>They went on to independently tackle more
            technical projects, including refactoring our graphing-library
            usage.
          </p>
        </div>
      </section>
      <section id="experience" class="section">
        <div class="section-heading">
          <h2>Experience</h2>
        </div>
        <Career />
      </section>
      <section
        class="section capabilities"
        aria-labelledby="capabilities-title"
      >
        <div>
          <h2 id="capabilities-title">Technical skills</h2>
        </div>
        <div class="capability-grid">
          <div>
            <h3>Product engineering</h3>
            <p>
              React, React Native, ReScript and TypeScript. Building interfaces
              and application logic together, with experience across web and
              mobile.
            </p>
          </div>
          <div>
            <h3>Integrations & reliability</h3>
            <p>
              APIs, webhooks, data modelling and transactional outboxes.
              Connecting services while accounting for failures and the people
              using them.
            </p>
          </div>
          <div>
            <h3>Planning & delivery</h3>
            <p>
              Provider evaluation, achievable milestones, stakeholder
              conversations and work allocation that reflects the team’s
              strengths.
            </p>
          </div>
          <div>
            <h3>Engineering foundations</h3>
            <p>
              Experience with Relay, Feathers.js, BigQuery, Java/Spring and
              automated testing. I seek infrastructure specialists’ input where
              operational decisions need deeper expertise.
            </p>
          </div>
        </div>
      </section>
      <section class="section personal" aria-labelledby="beyond-title">
        <div>
          <h2 id="beyond-title">Projects & interests</h2>
        </div>
        <div>
          <p>
            I built <a href="https://git-gif.vercel.app">Git gif</a> to turn
            videos into GIFs for pull requests, making it easier to show visual
            changes.
          </p>
          <p>
            I’m also building Loom, a personal Electron app that turns my
            preferred workflow with Codex and Claude into a repeatable process
            outside the terminal. It takes repository-based tasks through
            clarification, an explicit approval gate, implementation and
            human-plus-agent review. A planned website and server will make that
            workflow available remotely, with phone controls, push notifications
            and live WebSocket updates; those remote features are not yet
            implemented.
          </p>
          <p>
            Away from code, I enjoy cooking, from a meal for two to a table full
            of people. My{' '}
            <a href="/cooking/christmas/">Christmas dinner planner</a> brings a
            little engineering organisation to the kitchen.
          </p>
        </div>
      </section>
      <section id="contact" class="contact section">
        <h2>Contact</h2>
        <p>
          I’m open to conversations about engineering lead roles. I prefer
          remote work with occasional London get-togethers, and I’m also open to
          full-time office-based roles in Bristol or Cardiff.
        </p>
        <div class="contact-links">
          <a class="contact-email" href="mailto:resume@nfitton.com">
            resume@nfitton.com <span aria-hidden="true">↗</span>
          </a>
          <a class="text-link" href="/nicholas-fitton-cv.pdf" download>
            Download CV <span aria-hidden="true">↓</span>
          </a>
        </div>
      </section>
    </main>
    <footer class="footer">
      <span>Nicholas Fitton</span>
      <span>Chepstow, South Wales</span>
      <a href="#main">Back to top ↑</a>
    </footer>
  </div>
</Layout>
